EZ PERMIT STANDARDS ALTERATIONS- For alterations to an Existing One Family Dwelling as per attached standard. Deviations from this standard will result in permit revocation and require submission of construction plans. Separate permits are required for plumbing and electrical work and the installation of heating/cooling appliances. STRUCTURAL ALTERATION OR REPAIR IS EXPRESSLY PROHIBITED UNDER THIS PERMIT. PROHIBITED STRUCTURAL WORK INCLUDES ANY MODIFICATION TO EXTERIOR WALLS, PARTY WALLS, FLOOR/ROOF FRAMING OR FOUNDATIONS; INCLUDING UNDERPINNING, EXCAVATION, AND REMOVAL OF FOUNDATION SLAB.NO WORK MAY BE PERFORMED IN THE BASEMENT OR CELLAR.

Removal and installation of interior non-loadbearing partition walls and finishes throughout the property;
o New interior partition walls will consist of 2x4 studs @ 16” o.c and ½” thick GWB on each side.
Existing studs may also be used as desired by the Client;
o No exterior walls are planned to be constructed under this application. Exterior walls and insulation
shall remain as-is.
o First floor partitions will be used for a closet. The second floor shall consist of 1 bathrooms and 3
bedrooms.
• ceiling finishes shall consist of 5/8” GWB. At roof levels, replace insulation with R-49 insulation for any areas
impacted by the proposed work.
• construction of 1 bathroom including ASTM C630 water-resistant gypsum backer board, fixtures
, application of stucco or vinyl siding to exterior walls (as needed). No structural modifications to exterior walls
shall be performed under this application;
• installation of hard-wired, interconnected smoke and CO alarms in and just outside each bedroom and on each
occupied floor;
• installation of new windows units in existing openings. No new window openings are proposed;
• installation of kitchen finishes and casework;
• installation of new ductwork for HVAC units; and
• supplementary work only as allowed in the EZ Alteration Permit Standards.
